==============================================================================
K=2 rational-fit extrapolation test (reproducing/stress-testing
ATTEMPT.md Sec 4.1's claimed failure)
==============================================================================
3-param ansatz 1/3+a/n+b/n^2+c/n^3, fit on n=3,4,5: {a: -11/72, b: 37/72, c: 5/6}
  predicts n=6: 845/2592  actual: 44/135  MATCH=False
  predicts n=7: 2003/6174  actual: 143/441  MATCH=False
  CONFIRMED: 3-param fit fails to predict n=6,7, exactly as the document reports.

4-param ansatz 1/3+a/n+b/n^2+c/n^3+d/n^4, fit on n=3,4,5,6: {a: -61/360, b: 257/360, c: 1/20, d: 1}
  predicts n=7: 70069/216090  actual: 143/441  MATCH=False
  CONFIRMED: even a RICHER 4-parameter fit (using 4 exact data
  points, one more than the document's 3-param/3-point attempt)
  STILL fails to predict the 5th point. This corroborates -- does
  NOT contradict -- ATTEMPT.md Sec 4.1's claim that the true K=2
  joint closed form needs more structure than a small polynomial-
  in-1/n fit can recover from a handful of points. If anything
  this is stronger evidence for the difficulty than the document
  itself presents.
